### Verdict: CHERRY_PICKING

### Justification
The fact-check confirms that Donald Trump paid $750 in federal income taxes for both 2016 and 2017, as reported by [The New York Times](https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2020/sep/27/new-york-times-publishes-donald-trumps-tax-returns-election) and summarized by [NPR](https://www.npr.org/2020/09/27/917566141/trump-dismisses-new-york-times-reporting-that-he-paid-little-in-federal-income-t). Trump did make a similar public statement during a [2016 presidential debate](https://www.nbcnews.com/think/opinion/trump-tests-positive-covid-days-after-his-taxes-are-released-ncna1241730), saying "That makes me smart" in response to accusations of not paying taxes, though the exact phrasing in the claim is not documented. The low payments resulted from legal tax strategies, such as using business credits, and there is no evidence of illegal evasion. However, the claim is misleading because it cherry-picks these facts while omitting the context of their legality and misrepresents the quote by adding "I know how to game the system," creating a distorted impression.